Help For Split and Repeaters

l opens the control and reads its current state without changing it. Off reports only Off. When On, receive and transmit frequencies are reported. h reads this help. q keeps the current settings, announces Done and returns to top level.

Press l again to act on the live state. If On, it switches split/repeater operation Off and returns. If Off, it starts setup. Outside FM, enter the transmit frequency in MHz and press Enter. Receive stays on the selected VFO; setup replaces the other VFO frequency and mode. In FM, setup uses a saved band offset if available; otherwise enter a signed offset in hertz. A saved offset is never applied merely by opening the control.

At an input prompt, blank Enter or q then Enter cancels without changing settings. h then Enter explains the control. Type -600000 for Minus 600000 hertz; type 600000 or +600000 for Plus 600000 hertz. Changes are verified by reading the radio. No transmission is started. Unsupported or unreadable states are reported.

Repeated w at top level alternates normal status and live split/repeater details. If restoration fails, read the live receive/transmit details before using the radio; a failed restore is not confirmation of the previous settings. Model-specific choices and saved-offset configuration belong in the radio notes.

